<title>FINLAND: Finnish Nov EU-harmonised CPI rises 1.4 pct -SF.</title>
<headline>Finnish Nov EU-harmonised CPI rises 1.4 pct -SF.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Finnish consumer price index partially harmonised to European Union standards rose 1.4 percent year-on-year in November after a 1.3 percent rise in October, Statistics Finland (SF) said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>				Nov 1996	Oct 1996    Nov 1995</p>
<p> Yr/Yr			+1.4 pct	 +1.3 pct    +0.3 pct</p>
<p> Mth/Mth		    -0.1 pct	 +0.2 pct    -0.2 pct</p>
<p> Index (base 1994=100)   102.3	    102.5	 101.1</p>
<p>According to SF's regular national method of calculation, Finnish consumer prices fell 0.3 percent in November on October and rose 0.7 percent year-on-year, it said.</p>
<p>			     Nov 1996	 Oct 1996     Nov 1995</p>
<p> Yr/yr		     +0.7 pct	  +0.7 pct	+0.3 pct</p>
<p> Mth/mth		   -0.3 pct	  +0.2 pct	-0.3 pct</p>
<p> Index (base 1990=100)  112.7	     113.0	   112.9</p>
<p>Five economists' average forecast for the national CPI figure was for a 1.0 percent rise year-on-year and a 0 percent rise month-on-month.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358 - 9 - 680 50 245</p>
</text>
